To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the main objectives and break them down into sub-goals and tasks. Here's how the mission can be structured:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food                | Ensure food is delivered from the kitchen to the inpatient room.     | -                  | Achieve   | -        |
| G2      | Determine Delivery Method   | Decide whether to place food on the table or use the tray.           | FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2) | Query     | G1       |
| G2.1    | Check Inpatient Capability  | Verify if the inpatient can retrieve food from the tray.            | -                  | Query     | G2       |
| G2.2    | Check Companion/Nurse Availability | Verify if a companion or nurse is available to assist.             | -                  | Query     | G2       |
| G3      | Execute Delivery            | Deliver the food using the chosen method.                            | #                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G4      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes       | Ensure dirty dishes are retrieved from the room.                     | -                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G5      | Open Room Door              | Manage the opening of the room door for delivery and retrieval.      | FALLBACK(G5.1, G5.2) | Perform   | G1       |
| G5.1    | Robot Opens Door            | Have a robot open the door if no human is available.                 | -                  | Perform   | G5       |
| G5.2    | Human Opens Door            | Have a human open the door if available.                             | -                  | Perform   | G5       |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                   | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Room             | Move to the designated inpatient room.                               | AND      | Hospital Room     | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Place Food on Table          | Place the food directly on the room table.                           | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT3     | Indicate Meal for Retrieval  | Signal which meal should be retrieved by the inpatient.              | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT4     | Track Meal Retrieval         | Monitor when and where each meal is retrieved.                       | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT5     | Alert Wrong Meal Retrieval   | Notify if an incorrect meal is retrieved.                            | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT6     | Retrieve Dishes              | Collect dirty dishes from the room.                                  | AND      | Hospital Room     | [1, 2]           |
| AT7     | Signal Door Opening          | Indicate if a human can open the door when the robot arrives.        | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G4, G5 [AND]**
  - **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**
  - **G3 -> AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4, AT5 [AND]**
  - **G4 -> AT6 [AND]**
  - **G5 -> G5.1, G5.2 [OR]**

This structure ensures that all aspects of the mission are covered, from determining the delivery method to executing the delivery and handling dish retrieval, while considering the potential need for human cooperation.
